{"success":true,"message":"Response generated successfully.","data":{"requestId":"ca349990-06d8-4876-ab98-09ba1c846b0b","response":"The `prompt` function is used to display a message in the console and wait for user input before continuing execution of the program. It's commonly used in scripts or interactive programs.

Here is an example:

```javascript
console.log('Please enter your name:');
let userInput = prompt("What's your name?");

if (userInput) {
  console.log(`Hello, ${userInput}!`);
}
```

However, it's worth noting that `prompt` is a function of the browser's environment and doesn't work in Node.js or other server-side environments. If you try to run this code outside of a browser, you'll get an error because `prompt` isn't available.

In a browser context, after you enter your name in the prompt dialog box and press "OK," it will be echoed back on the screen along with a greeting that includes your name."},"timestamp":"2026-08-19T20:26:51.552453Z"}

